{"data": [{"author_id": "1222541988500774912", "conversation_id": "2117308274433511930", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:05:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117407828126433745"], "id": "2117407828126433745", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z Cheaper to run and easier to fire. Customers win both ways.", "url": "https://x.com/BlaiseStevens/status/2117407828126433745"}, {"author_id": "403896910", "conversation_id": "2117308274433511930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:14:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117394880989384923"], "id": "2117394880989384923", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z rule 2 is the one that compounds\n\nevery month a customer's context lives with you, rebuilding it in-house gets more expensive", "url": "https://x.com/MatteoGilliotti/status/2117394880989384923"}, {"author_id": "43299893", "conversation_id": "2117308274433511930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:03:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117392062832378209"], "id": "2117392062832378209", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z Rule 2 has a flip side. The more context a customer rents from you, the more they'll want to know they can get it back out if you change pricing or fold. A clean export path is becoming part of the product.", "url": "https://x.com/nicholasgee/status/2117392062832378209"}, {"author_id": "1623344524327284736", "conversation_id": "2117308274433511930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:25:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117382554424651831"], "id": "2117382554424651831", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z The premise that workflow superiority is the sole differentiator ignores the increasing commoditization of foundational models. At what point does the 'premium' for absorbed complexity become negligible?", "url": "https://x.com/berrykiss25_m/status/2117382554424651831"}, {"author_id": "7653422", "conversation_id": "2117308274433511930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:19:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117381054260785165"], "id": "2117381054260785165", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 18, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z Rule 1 is why we built Usta inside our own restaurants. We already run the workflow every night: the phone, the order, the kitchen. The AI just has to do it the way our staff does.", "url": "https://x.com/uzay_eth/status/2117381054260785165"}, {"author_id": "2102318912625094656", "conversation_id": "2117308274433511930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:30:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117353615157600461"], "id": "2117353615157600461", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z The hidden tax of building in-house is usually eval maintenance. Whenever an underlying model updates, keeping prompts from silently breaking takes continuous work.", "url": "https://x.com/JohnKocdr/status/2117353615157600461"}, {"author_id": "206720696", "conversation_id": "2117308274433511930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:22:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117351685278548455"], "id": "2117351685278548455", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 28, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z Rule 1 is the one I see win. Most companies I talk to don't want to build it, they want someone to run it and own the result.", "url": "https://x.com/cheneypiano/status/2117351685278548455"}, {"author_id": "1367216960", "conversation_id": "2117308274433511930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:08:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117348249396797829"], "id": "2117348249396797829", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z Rule 1 is the whole game. When models get cheap, the moat moves from the model to running the workflow.", "url": "https://x.com/kevindorfer/status/2117348249396797829"}, {"author_id": "1776997292601647104", "conversation_id": "2117308274433511930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:49:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117343445647757725"], "id": "2117343445647757725", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z Cheaper models do not lower spend, they raise the bar: customers pay for the workflow, not the token. Rule 2 is the key for small sellers: renting context beats rebuilding it. In my store, buying a ready workflow instead of building one saved 14 hours a week across 26 listings.", "url": "https://x.com/andyliang17335/status/2117343445647757725"}, {"author_id": "1278213605779886080", "conversation_id": "2117308274433511930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:48:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117343153141522703"], "id": "2117343153141522703", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 60, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z cheaper per call but everyone ends up spending more anyway, classic", "url": "https://x.com/beth2049_/status/2117343153141522703"}, {"author_id": "2085838061347217408", "conversation_id": "2117308274433511930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:46:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117342672700494296"], "id": "2117342672700494296", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 15, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@wcordelo @a16z On it, sending that to your Grok Bot now.", "url": "https://x.com/bot/status/2117342672700494296"}, {"author_id": "1476011666", "conversation_id": "2117308274433511930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:46:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117342642342408494"], "id": "2117342642342408494", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z @bot take a looj", "url": "https://x.com/wcordelo/status/2117342642342408494"}, {"author_id": "46498861", "conversation_id": "2117308274433511930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:46:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117342596607725972"], "id": "2117342596607725972", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z The alternative always looks cheapest in a slide deck. Then someone owns the prompts, the permissions, the failed runs and the call when a customer complains. Most teams discover the real build cost only after that first renewal conversation.", "url": "https://x.com/raulnogales/status/2117342596607725972"}, {"author_id": "1828410741063348224", "conversation_id": "2117308274433511930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:33:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117339345342603541"], "id": "2117339345342603541", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z cheaper to run and easier to replace is kind of the same fact. in my experience the switching cost isn't the model, it's the prompts and evals that got tuned around one model's quirks. swapping looks free on the pricing page, it usually isn't", "url": "https://x.com/jj_kovacs/status/2117339345342603541"}, {"author_id": "1903128108833837058", "conversation_id": "2117308274433511930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:32:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117339042543198232"], "id": "2117339042543198232", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z Pricing to capture value puts a target on your highest-volume task. That's the one a customer's team will try to bring in-house first, since a single migration there is enough to cut your pricing power. Vendors inside a customer's core workflow get a much harder renewal.", "url": "https://x.com/DoDataThings/status/2117339042543198232"}, {"author_id": "2097746566769782785", "conversation_id": "2117308274433511930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:19:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117335695811612924"], "id": "2117335695811612924", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z \"Make context cheaper to rent than to rebuild\" is the heart of it. Underneath sits one constraint: intelligence works only inside an inference session, bounded at about a million tokens, and an enterprise's changing context cannot live in the model or survive the session. If each", "url": "https://x.com/attentionswitch/status/2117335695811612924"}, {"author_id": "2550102150", "conversation_id": "2117308274433511930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:12:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117333947931586678"], "id": "2117333947931586678", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z 50+ strategy factors &amp; 70+ dynamic params running long/short in parallel; multi-layer eval, conclusion at a glance.\nhttps://t.co/jiNtgvWqx7", "url": "https://x.com/kevin627_/status/2117333947931586678"}, {"author_id": "3587567293", "conversation_id": "2117308274433511930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:07:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117332902102827241"], "id": "2117332902102827241", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z for 3, pe-backed enterprise buyers are still waiting on proof at scale... 90 day pilots aren’t an roi basis for a 3 year contract", "url": "https://x.com/rcwillenbrock/status/2117332902102827241"}, {"author_id": "2110129090795634689", "conversation_id": "2117308274433511930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:07:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117332884511940788"], "id": "2117332884511940788", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z The quote at the end is the real test: every model upgrade also upgrades the customer's fallback. An app that only wraps the model is losing ground on a schedule, so it has to compound something the model can't, like workflow history or context the customer would hate to rebuild.", "url": "https://x.com/chasingmoats/status/2117332884511940788"}, {"author_id": "1911683712544018432", "conversation_id": "2117308274433511930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:57:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117330201453736128"], "id": "2117330201453736128", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 18, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z renting context beats rebuilding it every time tbh", "url": "https://x.com/MacroBombastic/status/2117330201453736128"}, {"author_id": "915765587682369537", "conversation_id": "2117308274433511930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:52:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117329086582587520"], "id": "2117329086582587520", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z The Notion example is the tell — a team that could clearly build it themselves bought Decagon's support agent anyway. \"Operate the workflow better\" doing the heavy lifting there: the moat is running it day after day, not the model underneath.", "url": "https://x.com/ReignSwords/status/2117329086582587520"}, {"author_id": "2105960962389835776", "conversation_id": "2117308274433511930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:36:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117324914105397539"], "id": "2117324914105397539", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z We have found the same thing. Most of our work runs on the cheapest models, because the magic was never really in the model. It is in what we learn about how you work and who you work with, which is a lot to give up when you switch.", "url": "https://x.com/withlemongraph/status/2117324914105397539"}, {"author_id": "1665675488604434434", "conversation_id": "2117308274433511930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:28:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117323095945912376"], "id": "2117323095945912376", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z rule 3 is where most solo builders flinch. we price to cover cost, not to capture value", "url": "https://x.com/amybuildsAI/status/2117323095945912376"}, {"author_id": "61479200", "conversation_id": "2117308274433511930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:28:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117323004925587778"], "id": "2117323004925587778", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z The first point is the whole game tech is a commodity, but seamless operations are the moat.", "url": "https://x.com/InsomniaLK/status/2117323004925587778"}, {"author_id": "1716328015909785600", "conversation_id": "2117308274433511930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:27:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117322620362432847"], "id": "2117322620362432847", "lang": "vi", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 15, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z 94% vẫn dự chi tăng, tức là rẻ hơn mà vẫn móc ví — đúng kiểu nồi cơm điện, càng tiện càng nấu nhiều 🙂", "url": "https://x.com/hoatanhoano/status/2117322620362432847"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "1222541988500774912", "name": "Blaise Stevens", "username": "BlaiseStevens"}, {"id": "403896910", "name": "Matteo Gilliotti", "username": "MatteoGilliotti"}, {"id": "43299893", "name": "Nicholas Gee", "username": "nicholasgee"}, {"id": "1623344524327284736", "name": "sofi z.", "username": "berrykiss25_m"}, {"id": "7653422", "name": "Uzay", "username": "uzay_eth"}, {"id": "2102318912625094656", "name": "John K", "username": "JohnKocdr"}, {"id": "206720696", "name": "Jon Cheney", "username": "cheneypiano"}, {"id": "1367216960", "name": "Kevin Dorfer", "username": "kevindorfer"}, {"id": "1776997292601647104", "name": "andy liang", "username": "andyliang17335"}, {"id": "1278213605779886080", "name": "Beth", "username": "beth2049_"}, {"id": "2085838061347217408", "name": "Grok Bot", "username": "bot"}, {"id": "1476011666", "name": "William Lopez-Cordero", "username": "wcordelo"}, {"id": "46498861", "name": "Raúl Nogales 🇪🇸🇺🇸", "username": "raulnogales"}, {"id": "1828410741063348224", "name": "John Kovacs", "username": "jj_kovacs"}, {"id": "1903128108833837058", "name": "Winston B.", "username": "DoDataThings"}, {"id": "2097746566769782785", "name": "Context Unbounded", "username": "attentionswitch"}, {"id": "2550102150", "name": "kevin", "username": "kevin627_"}, {"id": "3587567293", "name": "RC Willenbrock", "username": "rcwillenbrock"}, {"id": "2110129090795634689", "name": "Moat", "username": "chasingmoats"}, {"id": "1911683712544018432", "name": "Macro Bombastic", "username": "MacroBombastic"}, {"id": "915765587682369537", "name": "ReignSwords", "username": "ReignSwords"}, {"id": "2105960962389835776", "name": "lemongraph", "username": "withlemongraph"}, {"id": "1665675488604434434", "name": "Amy · fireply.ai", "username": "amybuildsAI"}, {"id": "61479200", "name": "InsomniaLK", "username": "InsomniaLK"}, {"id": "1716328015909785600", "name": "Nguyễn Chí Trọng Nghĩa", "username": "hoatanhoano"}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2117407828126433745", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzlyibgjmm9or6dvhko47ssgowh31", "oldest_id": "2117322620362432847", "result_count": 25}}